\title{Higher Algebra in Simplicial Homotopy Type Theory}
\author{robschellingerhout}
\taxon{Reference}
\date{2026}
\meta{venue}{[[uutrecht]]}
\meta{external}{https://studenttheses.uu.nl/handle/20.500.12932/52586}

\subtree{
\taxon{Abstract}

\p{
We study symmetric monoidal #{∞}-categories and #{∞}-operads in the setting of
simplicial homotopy type theory. We define these notions within this formalism and
show that they agree with [Lurie](jacoblurie)’s definitions in the models. Moreover,
we use Lurie’s methods to show that Cartesian products are symmetric monoidal, and we
show that Lurie’s construction of the Day convolution of #{∞}-operads yields an
#{∞}-operad. Along the way, we develop the general theory of synthetic
#{∞}-categories further, by proving new characterizations and closure properties of
cocartesian families, by proving the functoriality of limits and Kan-extensions, and
by developing the theory of factorization systems.
}
}

